Given equation:

122 &divide; 4 + 65 × 5 - 41 = ?

Interchanging operators:

When &lsquo;+&rsquo; and &lsquo;&minus;&rsquo; are interchanged and &lsquo;×&rsquo; and &lsquo;&divide;&rsquo; are interchanged, the new equation becomes:

122 × 4 &minus; 65 &divide; 5 + 41

Solution:

Following the order of operations (BODMAS/PEMDAS):

= 122 × 4 - 65 &divide; 5 + 41

= 488 - 13 + 41

= 475 + 41 = 516

Hence, the correct answer is **"Option 3".**

